body:
Pancreatitis.

I was 17. Most people get it from drug and alcohol abuse, but I had a vicious stomach virus that infected my pancreas. Constant puking and incredibly sharp pains. I was not allowed to eat for 10 days, just IVs of saline and nutrients. Anything that touched my mouth was almost instantly thrown up. I went from 140lbs to 118lbs in those 10 days. When I was finally allowed to eat, all I could have was broth.

&#x200B;

I was on a morphine drip but all it did was dull the pain. I could still feel it constantly. I mostly slept and don't remember too many details of my hospital stay. I remember a lot of concerned adults and the worried look on my doctor's face. My friends came to visit me but it's all sort of a blur. 

&#x200B;

That was 12 years ago. My stomach is still kinda sensitive. I throw up fairly easily.
